  "text": "The field faces uncertainty because some scholars, rooted in older, more established areas, view it with skepticism. This doubt is not just about status; there is a genuine problem of lacking a shared theory, leaving us unclear about our identity and purpose. Opinions differ on whether a formal theory is needed now. A group of researchers proposes various conceptual frameworks, while others argue that the discipline should evolve organically through its own work, letting practice shape methods. They note that scholarly techniques develop from repeated critique of actual work aimed at fixing its flaws. Although practical achievements deserve respect, ignoring theory altogether seems unwise; theoretical ideas, treated as proposals rather than strict rules, can clarify concepts, suggest useful categories, and generate promising hypotheses. Ultimately, the field must justify itself beyond narrow literary or purely statistical approaches."
